.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Extends \fBIFastType\fP with typed access to the underlying storage value\&. Implementations define how the raw value is represented (e\&.g\&., uint, ulong, ushort, double, long), enabling bit‑level inspection and mutation of arbitrary numeric formats\&. 

This interface is type‑agnostic and supports both integer and floating‑point representations\&. For floating‑point types, the bit operations apply to the raw IEEE‑754 encoding (or custom formats such as \fR\fBHalf16\fP\fP)\&. 

.PP
Additional operations include: 

.PP
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBOne’s complement\fP (\fBCmpOne\fP) — invert all bits\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBTwo’s complement\fP (\fBCmpTwo\fP) — invert all bits and add one\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBMasking\fP (\fBMask\fP) — apply a bitmask using AND\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBMask creation\fP (\fBCreateMask\fP) — generate a contiguous bitmask of arbitrary length\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBCombination\fP (\fBCombine\fP) — merge two bit patterns using OR\&.   
.PP

.PP
Implementations must guarantee that all operations modify or inspect the underlying value deterministically and without hidden conversions\&. 

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP The underlying storage type (e\&.g\&., uint, ulong, ushort, double, long)\&. 
.RE
.PP

